(formula "IV AUT" "M3" "=Lab!I14")
(cell "IV AUT" "N1" "AUT, either but not both: the lamp lit where exactly one of a and b is 1.")
(cell "IV AUT" "N2" "Given NON-ET, NON, ET, and VEL, proven at III, =MAX(x,y). Write y in J3.")
(cell "IV AUT" "N3" "Latin is said to keep two ors, vel the inclusive and aut the exclusive; the Stanford Encyclopedia called that a myth in 2016.")
(cell "IV AUT" "N4" "Aut has inclusive uses too. Here it is exclusive anyway, and VEL and NON-ET together nearly say it.")
(cell "IV AUT" "N7" "Space toggles the switch the selection stands on, 1 and 0 set it, a click toggles it; T tests, R resets, N and P move.")
(cell "IV AUT" "N10" "A switch or a lamp written over is lost until Load, which loads every level afresh: R writes values, never a formula.")
(formula "IV AUT" "N8" "=\"Gates \"&Lab!E14&\"; the budget 5, the least known 3: \"&Lab!H14")
